<!DOCTYPE html>
<!-- Shown as the final ("conclusion") screen of the macOS installer. build_release_package.sh
     substitutes <fastsurfer> with FastSurfer<version> and copies the result into the installer
     resources; edit_distribution.py registers it as text/html, so the links below are clickable.
     Keep it short: the pane is narrow and scrolling is easy to miss. -->
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<style>
  :root { color-scheme: light dark; }
  body {
    font: 13px -apple-system, "Helvetica Neue", sans-serif;
    line-height: 1.45;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 2px 4px 12px;
  }
  h2 {
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(127, 127, 127, 0.25);
    font-size: 13px;
    margin: 20px 0 5px;
    padding-top: 12px;
  }
  p, ul { margin: 4px 0; }
  ul { padding-left: 17px; }
  pre {
    background: rgba(127, 127, 127, 0.14);
    border-radius: 5px;
    font: 11px ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace;
    margin: 5px 0;
    padding: 6px 8px;
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    word-break: break-word;
  }
  code { font: 11px ui-monospace, Menlo, monospace; }
  .muted { opacity: 0.75; }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<p><b>FastSurfer is installed in /Applications/<fastsurfer></b></p>

<h2>Open the FastSurfer console</h2>
<p>Double-click <b><fastsurfer></b> in your Applications folder. It opens a Terminal window with
everything set up, recognizable by the <code>(<fastsurfer>)</code> prompt prefix.</p>
<p class="muted">Any bash or zsh Terminal window works too:</p>
<pre>source /Applications/<fastsurfer>/macos_setup_fastsurfer.sh</pre>
<p class="muted">Your shell profile is not modified, so this is needed once per window.</p>

<h2>Run FastSurfer</h2>
<p>Segmentation only (no FreeSurfer license needed):</p>
<pre>run_fastsurfer.sh --seg_only --sid &lt;subject_id&gt; \
  --t1 /full/path/to/t1.nii.gz --sd /full/path/to/output</pre>
<p>Full pipeline, including surfaces:</p>
<pre>run_fastsurfer.sh --sid &lt;subject_id&gt; --fs_license ~/fs_license.txt \
  --t1 /full/path/to/t1.nii.gz --sd /full/path/to/output</pre>
<p class="muted">Give <code>--t1</code> and <code>--sd</code> as full paths; a relative
<code>--t1</code> is rejected. The Apple GPU is used automatically where available.</p>

<h2>FreeSurfer license</h2>
<p>The surface pipeline (and <code>--tal_reg</code> for eTIV) needs a free FreeSurfer license:
<a href="https://surfer.nmr.mgh.harvard.edu/registration.html">register here</a>, save the file in
your home directory and pass it with <code>--fs_license</code>. It cannot live inside the bundled
FreeSurfer, which is installed as <code>root</code>.</p>

<h2>Uninstalling</h2>
<p>Drag both <b><fastsurfer></b> and <b><fastsurfer>.app</b> to the Trash; macOS asks for your
password. Nothing is installed elsewhere, so that is all there is to remove.</p>

<h2>Documentation</h2>
<ul>
  <li><a href="https://deep-mi.org/FastSurfer/stable/overview/INSTALL.html#macos">macOS installation and usage</a></li>
  <li><a href="https://deep-mi.org/FastSurfer/stable/">FastSurfer documentation</a></li>
  <li><a href="https://github.com/Deep-MI/FastSurfer/issues">Report a problem</a></li>
</ul>

</body>
</html>
